<title>GREECE: DELOS, INTERNATIONAL LEAD GREEK BALANCED FUNDS IN H1.</title>
<headline>DELOS, INTERNATIONAL LEAD GREEK BALANCED FUNDS IN H1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delos and International mutual</p>
<p>funds were the top runners among Greece's 16 balanced funds in</p>
<p>the first half of 1997 with returns of 66.64 and 49.26 percent,</p>
<p>respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>Delos stood out as the only equity-income fund to better the</p>
<p>bourse's benchmark index in the first half.</p>
<p>The Athens stock exchange's general share index started the</p>
<p>year at 954.54 and gained 563.97 points or 59.08 percent to</p>
<p>1,518.51 points in the six months to June 30.</p>
<p>Second-best performer, International, more than tripled the</p>
<p>number of its shares in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>Balanced fund assets under management reached 67.5 billion</p>
<p>drachmas in end-June, up 67.75 percent since the beginning of</p>
<p>the year and down 1.29 percent on May.</p>
<p>They made up 1.68 percent of the mutual fund industry's</p>
<p>total assets which rose to 5.41 trillion drachmas in the first</p>
<p>half of 1997, an increase of 41.84 percent.</p>
